## Why This Is Asked
Tests an advanced multi-account security pattern: tenant isolation, key management, and rapid containment in a live streaming data pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account IAM roles with MFA
- Per-tenant CMKs and rotation policies
- Explicit trust conditions (aws:SourceAccount, aws:SourceArn, aws:RequestedRegion)
- PrivateLink/VPCE for data-plane isolation
- Immutable audit trails via CloudTrail across regions
- Breach-testing and automated containment

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-${aws:userid}-data/*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-${aws:userid}-data"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:SourceAccount": "${aws:SourceAccount}",
          "aws:RequestedRegion": ["us-east-1", "us-west-2"]
        },
        "ArnEquals": {
          "aws:SourceArn": "arn:aws:iam::${aws:SourceAccount}:role/tenant-analytics-role"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design tenant isolation in a multi-account AWS data platform using modern controls (S3 Access Points, ABAC, cross-account roles) and an automated containment workflow.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant S3 Access Points and isolated buckets
- ABAC with aws:PrincipalTag for tenant isolation
- Cross-account roles for analytics with least privilege
- Automated containment: CMK rotation, token revocation, data quarantine
- Immutable logging and breach test planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Conceptual IAM policy snippet for per-tenant access via ABAC
const policy = {
  Version: "2012-10-17",
  Statement: [
    {
      Effect: "Allow",
      Action: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      Resource: [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}/*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}"
      ],
      Condition: {
        StringEquals: {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the breach containment flow end-to-end?
- What failure modes could defeat auto-containment and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of time-bound access, cross-account trust, and auditable controls for external data sharing in a single AWS account context.

## Key Concepts

- STS AssumeRole with short-lived session
- IAM trust policies and cross-account access
- S3 Access Points and bucket policies for granular prefix access
- TLS enforcement, IP allow-lists, PrivateLink/VPCE
- KMS encryption and CloudTrail/S3 access logs

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::PARTNER_ACCOUNT_ID:root"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": "true"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket/your-prefix/*"],
      "Condition": {"IpAddress": {"aws:SourceIp": "203.0.113.0/24"}, "Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test and verify revocation works automatically after 14 days?
- What logging and alerting would you add to detect misuse or anomalies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical familiarity with cross-account access, least privilege via Access Points, and rapid containment. It also probes policy craft, ABAC usage, and automated incident response.

## Key Concepts
- S3 Access Points and per-tenant isolation
- VPC endpoints and endpoint policies for private access
- ABAC with tenant tags for cross-account trusts
- Cross-account roles, key management, and rapid containment workflows

## Code Example
```json
// S3 bucket policy snippet (deny public access)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {"StringNotEquals": {"aws:SourceVpce": "vpce-0123456789abcdef"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
// Example endpoint policy (allow from Data/Compute accounts only)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": ["arn:aws:iam::111111111111:role/tenantComputeRole"]},
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tested ABAC-based access across accounts before deployment?
- What monitoring alerts ensure detection and containment of exfiltration attempts within 60 seconds?
